GROUPED QUANTIZATION at g=128, registered in experiments/prereg_quant_grouped.json (sha256 953d354e0ac5...). Same estimator, same cells, same probe set as F187; the ONLY change is granularity -- one scale per (output row, group of 128 input channels) instead of one per row. That is the granularity GPTQ, AWQ and bitsandbytes quantize at.  gpt-neo-125m@int4g128: 0.0022 against per-channel 0.0; feature-A keeps 5 of 279 (0.0179).  pythia-410m@int4g128: 0.1812 against per-channel 0.0098; feature-A keeps 3 of 8 (0.375).  pythia-410m-deduped@int4g128: 0.2563 against per-channel 0.0103; feature-A keeps 1 of 8 (0.125).  rwkv-4-430m-pile@int4g128: 0.5297 against per-channel 0.4286; feature-A keeps 261 of 470 (0.5553).  mamba-370m-hf@int4g128: 0.0404 against per-channel 0.0151; feature-A keeps 2 of 711 (0.0028).  gpt-neo-125m@int8g128: 0.8175 against per-channel 0.7734; feature-A keeps 250 of 279 (0.8961).  pythia-410m@int8g128: 0.9121 against per-channel 0.9018; feature-A keeps 8 of 8 (1.0).  pythia-410m-deduped@int8g128: 0.9475 against per-channel 0.8966; feature-A keeps 7 of 8 (0.875).  rwkv-4-430m-pile@int8g128: 0.9608 against per-channel 0.9508; feature-A keeps 462 of 470 (0.983).  mamba-370m-hf@int8g128: 0.5498 against per-channel 0.4606; feature-A keeps 532 of 711 (0.7482).  KG1 FIRES: grouped 4-bit reaches 0.1812, still at or below the 0.6355 the corpus manipulation produces. GRANULARITY IS NOT WHAT KILLED 4-BIT. The paper's full-precision scoping stands unchanged, and the remaining hope for 4-bit rests entirely on calibration, which this run does not implement.  WHAT REMAINS OWED, unchanged and narrowed rather than closed: grouping is not calibration. GPTQ compensates quantization error with a Hessian-based update and AWQ with activation-aware scaling, and neither is implemented here. The owed item survives as calibration alone; activation quantization and real serving stacks are untouched. REFUSALS: no p-value on five cells; no adjustment of the group size, bit widths or comparison point; feature A reported as a kept fraction and never as a Hamming count.

